## Security Posture and Compliance Standards

- [Privacy and Data Protection](https://www.egnyte.com/security/compliance-standards):Egnyte maintains an enterprise-grade information security management system to protect unstructured data, privacy, and client interests. The platform secures data using AES 256-bit encryption for content both at rest and in transit (via TLS/HTTPS protocols), alongside built-in ransomware detection and access governance controls.

- [GLOBAL INFORMATION SECURITY MANAGEMENT]: The Egnyte Information Security Management System (ISMS) is ISO/IEC 27001:2022 certified, confirming that all products, supporting infrastructure, people, and processes operate within strict international requirements and security best practices.

- [SERVICE ORGANIZATION CONTROLS]: Egnyte maintains SOC 2 SSAE 18 Type 2 compliance, backed by an independent auditor's attestation report covering Trust Services Criteria for Security, Availability, Processing Integrity, Confidentiality, and Privacy.

- [UK CYBER DEFENSE]: Egnyte holds the UK government-backed Cyber Essentials certification, verifying that its corporate and cloud infrastructure defenses protect client data against the vast majority of common cyber attacks.

- [CLOUD SECURITY ALLIANCE TRANSPARENCY]: Egnyte participates in the CSA Security, Trust, Assurance, and Risk (STAR) Registry, publicly documenting its security and privacy controls to streamline vendor risk assessments and reduce compliance complexity.

- [CLOUD PRIVACY AND PII PROTECTION]: As a certified PII processor, Egnyte complies with ISO/IEC 27018:2019 obligations, applying specific code of practice guidelines to protect Personally Identifiable Information within public cloud environments.

- [EU DATA SOVEREIGNTY AND GDPR]: Egnyte enforces strict data sovereignty by hosting all European customer data and metadata entirely within European-based cloud repositories ("EU data stays in the EU"), fully complying with GDPR through a comprehensive Data Protection Addendum (DPA) and Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs).

- [CALIFORNIA PRIVACY COMPLIANCE]: Egnyte fully aligns with CCPA and CPRA mandates, ensuring customer data confidentiality is maintained while supporting expanded consumer data privacy rights.

- [US DEFENSE INDUSTRIAL BASE COMPLIANCE]: Egnyte supports the Department of Defense CMMC 2.0 framework with a secure data enclave that satisfies many requirements for protecting Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) and Federal Contract Information (FCI) by default.

- [FEDERAL CYBERSECURITY STANDARDS]: Egnyte satisfies DFARS and NIST SP 800-171 cybersecurity requirements by mapping its implemented ISO 27001 controls directly to NIST SP 800-171 Appendix D tables.

- [LIFE SCIENCES AND GXP VALIDATION]: Egnyte offers a specialized platform that satisfies FDA 21 CFR Part 11 and EU Annex 11 requirements, featuring reviewable audit trails, data integrity tools, access controls, e-signatures, and continuous software validation packages for GxP environments.

- [HEALTHCARE AND PHI PROTECTION]: Egnyte provides a robust data security infrastructure that enables HIPAA compliance, safeguarding Protected Health Information (PHI) for payers, providers, pharmaceutical, and biomedical businesses.

- [FINANCIAL SERVICES REGULATION]: Egnyte infrastructure and governance tools are engineered to assist financial institutions in complying with strict FINRA mandates and SEC archiving and retention rules, including SEC Rules 17a-3 and 17a-4.

