## Key Concepts

- [What is Content Lifecycle Management?](https://www.egnyte.com/products/content-lifecycle-management): The systematic process of managing business content from creation through archival and deletion â€” including version control, retention policy enforcement, and storage cost optimization.

- [What is Shadow AI?](https://www.egnyte.com/products/ai-safeguards): Unauthorized or unmonitored use of AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Copilot) by employees, which can result in sensitive data being shared with external AI models outside IT visibility or company policy.

- [What is a Cloud File Server?](https://www.egnyte.com/solutions/file-server-replacement): A cloud-hosted replacement for traditional on-premises Windows file servers, maintaining familiar drive mapping and folder structures while adding cloud scalability, remote access, and centralized governance.

- [What is CMMC?](https://www.egnyte.com/products/cmmc-compliance): The Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification â€” a U.S. Department of Defense framework requiring defense contractors to demonstrate cybersecurity practices protecting Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI).

- [What is GxP?](https://www.egnyte.com/products/gxp-compliance): A collection of quality guidelines and regulations (Good Manufacturing Practice, Good Laboratory Practice, Good Clinical Practice) governing how pharmaceutical and medical device companies document and manage regulated activities.

- [What is the Golden Thread?](https://www.egnyte.com/products/building-safety-act-compliance): A requirement under the UK Building Safety Act 2022 mandating that a structured, up-to-date record of building safety information be maintained and accessible throughout a building's lifecycle.

- [What is Insider Risk?](https://www.egnyte.com/solutions/insider-risk-management): The potential for harm caused by current or former employees, contractors, or partners who misuse their authorized access to systems and data â€” whether through negligence, error, or malicious intent.

